      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 1\n",
        "\n",
        "1. __Take time to get to know your data.__ Based on some initial exploration, identify 3 variables in the dataset you think will have strong predictive ability for determining if a house was built before 1980. Explain/justify the reasoning behind your guesses (for example with plots).\n",
        "\n",
        "I had 50 columns to choose from.\n",
        "For the 3 I'll use:\n",
        "- livearea\n",
        "- gartype_Att\n",
        "- sprice\n",
        "I chose these becuase after a bit of research I found that homes are larger nowaday, they are way more likely to have an attached garage, and they are going to be more expensive.\n",
        "\n",
        "Upon further testing and consideration I changed my 3 to be:\n",
        "- livearea\n",
        "- finbsmnt\n",
        "- gartype \n",
        "\n",
        "Houses are bigger nowadays. Houses nowadays have finished basements. And houses nowadays have attached garages.\n",
        "\n",
        "Upon even more testing and further consideration, I found no plausible way to train a model with an accuracy of at least 90%, only using three of the columns. That is, of course, excluding the year column itself, which would give an accuracy of 100%. I couldn't find anywhere in the assignment that said we couldn't use it, but I'm assuming we can't use it.\n",
        "In the final version I used [\n",
        "    'quality_C', \n",
        "    'gartype_Att', \n",
        "    'arcstyle_ONE-STORY', \n",
        "    'livearea', \n",
        "    'stories', \n",
        "    'numbaths', \n",
        "    'sprice', \n",
        "    'basement',\n",
        "    'arcstyle_TWO-STORY', \n",
        "    'quality_B', \n",
        "    'finbsmnt'\n",
        "] and I got an accuracy of 92.1% with XGBoost.\n"
      ],
      "id": "17516294"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "display(df.sample(20))\n",
        "\n",
        "df.columns\n",
        "df.shape\n",
        "\n",
        "# Charts to back up my claims:\n",
        "plot_df = df.with_columns(\n",
        "    pl.when(pl.col(\"before1980\") == 1)\n",
        "    .then(pl.lit(\"Pre-1980\"))\n",
        "    .otherwise(pl.lit(\"Post-1980\"))\n",
        "    .alias(\"era\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    ggplot(plot_df, aes(x=\"era\", y=\"livearea\"))\n",
        "    + geom_boxplot()\n",
        "    + labs(title=\"Living Area by Before/After 1980\", x=\"Era\", y=\"Living Area (sqft)\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    ggplot(plot_df, aes(x=\"era\", y=\"finbsmnt\"))\n",
        "    + geom_boxplot()\n",
        "    + labs(title=\"Finished Basement Sqft by Before/After 1980\", x=\"Era\", y=\"Finished Basement (sqft)\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    ggplot(plot_df, aes(x=\"gartype_Att\", fill=\"era\"))\n",
        "    + geom_bar(position=\"fill\")\n",
        "    + labs(title=\"Attached Garage by Before/After 1980\", x=\"Attached Garage\", y=\"Proportion\", fill=\"Era\")\n",
        ")"
      ],
