      "source": [
        "## QUESTION 2\n",
        "\n",
        "1. __Build a classification model labeling houses as being built “before 1980” or “during or after 1980”.__ Your goal is to reach or exceed 90% accuracy. Report your final model choice and any other model parameters you may have tweaked (train-test split ratio, tuning parameters, etc).  \n",
        "\n",
        "RandomForest can get up to about 87.2% accuracy using 'livearea', 'basement', and 'arcstyle_ONE-STORY'\n",
        "But XGBoost takes the cake when you give it more then 3 inputs. You get an accuracy of 92.1% with 11 columns. \n",
        "Interesting note but when you give XGBoost only 3 columns it only gets 85.6% accuracy. \n",
        "In summary, XGBoost beats RandomForest when given 11 inputs by 0.1% in accuracy, but RandomForest beats XGBoost when given only 3 inputs by 6.5% in accuracy."
      ],
      "id": "e3a80ea3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_columns = ['livearea', 'basement', 'arcstyle_ONE-STORY'] \n",
        "\n",
        "x = df.select(feature_columns).to_numpy()\n",
        "y = df.select('before1980').to_numpy().ravel()\n",
        "\n",
        "x_train, x_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(x, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "model = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
        "    n_estimators=2000,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=-1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "model.fit(x_train, y_train)\n",
        "print(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_test, model.predict(x_test)))\n"
      ],
      "id": "67319f6a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
